WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.208 --> 00:00:03.299
I've never vlogged
before, so this is funny.

00:00:03.299 --> 00:00:04.925
I hope I'm doing this right.

00:00:04.925 --> 00:00:06.920
(upbeat music)

00:00:06.920 --> 00:00:09.920
I moved to Los Angeles from
Oklahoma a few years ago,

00:00:09.920 --> 00:00:12.941
and I just had a really
deep desire to be a director

00:00:12.941 --> 00:00:15.472
but was utterly terrified to break into

00:00:15.472 --> 00:00:17.670
such a male-dominated industry.

00:00:17.670 --> 00:00:19.912
I was very lucky to get
an internship at Buzzfeed,

00:00:19.912 --> 00:00:22.000
and after about a year total of begging

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:23.461
to be on the creative team,

00:00:23.461 --> 00:00:24.661
they finally let me.

00:00:24.661 --> 00:00:25.901
I get to go around the country

00:00:25.901 --> 00:00:28.131
and direct videos, which
is an absolute dream.

00:00:28.131 --> 00:00:30.072
And so this weekend I'm going to Chicago.

00:00:30.072 --> 00:00:31.880
While I'm there I'm going to be vlogging

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:33.872
five pieces of advice about what it's like

00:00:33.872 --> 00:00:37.091
to be a woman breaking into
a male-dominated field.

00:00:37.091 --> 00:00:38.341
Binks!

00:00:38.341 --> 00:00:39.519
Hi, honey.

00:00:39.519 --> 00:00:41.680
I'm procrastinating packing for Chicago

00:00:41.680 --> 00:00:43.640
so instead I'm gonna do my first vlog.

00:00:43.640 --> 00:00:44.911
My first piece of advice

00:00:44.911 --> 00:00:47.131
is to trust your vision.

00:00:47.131 --> 00:00:48.849
It means trusting the vision that you have

00:00:48.849 --> 00:00:50.640
for yourself and for your future.

00:00:50.640 --> 00:00:53.971
For years I could not
call myself a director,

00:00:53.971 --> 00:00:56.451
because I felt like an imposter.

00:00:56.451 --> 00:00:58.640
I have pink hair, I'm very young,

00:00:58.640 --> 00:01:00.512
you know...I'm not a dude.

00:01:00.512 --> 00:01:02.261
After awhile I was like,
"This is really silly

00:01:02.261 --> 00:01:05.061
because I am a director,
and that's what I do."

00:01:05.061 --> 00:01:07.992
Once I started trusting that
vision and really believing it,

00:01:07.992 --> 00:01:09.320
other people started believing it.

00:01:09.320 --> 00:01:12.261
It starts with you believing
it first and trusting in that,

00:01:12.261 --> 00:01:13.811
and then the rest will follow.

00:01:13.811 --> 00:01:15.900
Okay, will someone come pack for me,

00:01:15.900 --> 00:01:17.741
because I really hate packing.

00:01:17.741 --> 00:01:20.908
(light, upbeat music)

00:01:22.840 --> 00:01:25.352
Good morning from Chicago.

00:01:25.352 --> 00:01:28.158
I'm up very early, getting
ready for my shoot.

00:01:28.158 --> 00:01:31.021
Number two is you take
care of yourself first.

00:01:31.021 --> 00:01:32.571
Just because you are a woman,

00:01:32.571 --> 00:01:34.400
perhaps in a male-dominated field,

00:01:34.400 --> 00:01:37.131
that doesn't mean that
you can't be a woman.

00:01:37.131 --> 00:01:39.712
On set, I'm in tennis shoes,
my hair is usually up,

00:01:39.712 --> 00:01:41.560
I'm usually very sweaty and disgusting.

00:01:41.560 --> 00:01:43.571
But whenever there is a break

00:01:43.571 --> 00:01:46.400
I usually do go to the restroom
and reapply my lipstick.

00:01:46.400 --> 00:01:47.341
I used to be a little embarrassed

00:01:47.341 --> 00:01:48.781
about that kind of stuff, but not anymore.

00:01:48.781 --> 00:01:53.061
Whenever I travel, I bring
my whole skin-care routine.

00:01:53.061 --> 00:01:55.840
I bring my Whips, my Olay Whips.

00:01:55.840 --> 00:01:57.851
It just makes me feel more confident,

00:01:57.851 --> 00:01:59.409
and I think it makes me a better director

00:01:59.409 --> 00:02:01.872
whenever I show up feeling good.

00:02:01.872 --> 00:02:03.821
Whatever it is that you
like, you should do that,

00:02:03.821 --> 00:02:04.960
and you should take care of yourself,

00:02:04.960 --> 00:02:08.192
because those are gonna
yield the best results.

00:02:08.192 --> 00:02:09.941
Number three: Plan ahead.

00:02:09.941 --> 00:02:12.209
Unfortunately, I think as a woman,

00:02:12.209 --> 00:02:14.859
if you are not fully buttoned up it's very

00:02:14.859 --> 00:02:18.931
easy for other people to assume
that you are underqualified.

00:02:18.931 --> 00:02:20.610
Do the research, do your homework,

00:02:20.610 --> 00:02:22.200
take the detailed notes,

00:02:22.200 --> 00:02:24.760
whatever it is you need to
do to go above and beyond.

00:02:24.760 --> 00:02:27.192
Don't ever give anyone a reason to say

00:02:27.192 --> 00:02:29.451
that you don't know what you're doing.

00:02:29.451 --> 00:02:31.470
Because you do.

00:02:31.470 --> 00:02:33.021
(water splashing)

00:02:33.021 --> 00:02:34.072
I wanted to give my
fourth piece of advice,

00:02:34.072 --> 00:02:35.420
which is to be vocal,

00:02:35.420 --> 00:02:39.400
and I think this one can be
tough for women, especially me.

00:02:39.400 --> 00:02:40.781
If someone is speaking over you

00:02:40.781 --> 00:02:44.571
or steamrolling a task
that you were assigned to,

00:02:44.571 --> 00:02:46.729
it is okay to say, "Hey, excuse me,

00:02:46.729 --> 00:02:48.371
"I actually wasn't finished speaking."

00:02:48.371 --> 00:02:52.839
If you do that in a polite,
professional manner,

00:02:52.839 --> 00:02:55.381
and they're offended by you
speaking up for yourself,

00:02:55.381 --> 00:02:56.541
that's not your problem.

00:02:56.541 --> 00:02:58.851
Because if you don't speak
up for yourself, who's gonna?

00:02:58.851 --> 00:03:02.018
(upbeat techno music)

00:03:03.590 --> 00:03:05.451
I just got home from Chicago.

00:03:05.451 --> 00:03:07.262
I am running on three hours of sleep,

00:03:07.262 --> 00:03:10.320
actually very surprised that
my skin looks this good.

00:03:10.320 --> 00:03:12.651
But I wanted to give you
my final piece of advice.

00:03:12.651 --> 00:03:14.710
Number five would to be listen well.

00:03:14.710 --> 00:03:17.552
I personally have kind of a
bad habit of walking around

00:03:17.552 --> 00:03:19.486
a little bit like, "I know what I'm doing,

00:03:19.486 --> 00:03:21.157
"and I don't need help from anybody."

00:03:21.157 --> 00:03:23.446
You never know when someone else's idea

00:03:23.446 --> 00:03:26.366
is going to help you,
or teach you a lesson,

00:03:26.366 --> 00:03:28.398
or make your idea even better.

00:03:28.398 --> 00:03:30.038
And remember: It's okay to say no.

00:03:30.038 --> 00:03:30.871
Listen first,

00:03:30.871 --> 00:03:34.188
and then if someone's idea
doesn't align with what you want,

00:03:34.188 --> 00:03:35.376
then you can say no.

00:03:35.376 --> 00:03:38.348
I would just encourage always
being humble and open-minded,

00:03:38.348 --> 00:03:40.457
because no one's ever gotten very far

00:03:40.457 --> 00:03:42.024
in this world all alone.

00:03:42.024 --> 00:03:43.677
(upbeat, happy music)

00:03:43.677 --> 00:03:45.135
This all comes straight from my mother.

00:03:45.135 --> 00:03:47.007
These are all things that she has told me.

00:03:47.007 --> 00:03:49.156
I wanna leave this video just hoping that

00:03:49.156 --> 00:03:50.694
some of what I've said can help

00:03:50.694 --> 00:03:53.197
at least one other
young woman in the world

00:03:53.197 --> 00:03:55.695
who has big dreams and wants to break into

00:03:55.695 --> 00:03:57.607
some sort of male-dominated industry,

00:03:57.607 --> 00:03:59.985
or any industry, whatever
it is you wanna do.

00:03:59.985 --> 00:04:00.818
I hope some of...

00:04:00.818 --> 00:04:03.054
I'm getting emotional!

00:04:03.054 --> 00:04:05.647
I did not think that would happen.

00:04:05.647 --> 00:04:07.706
Keep empowering one another,

00:04:07.706 --> 00:04:10.367
keep being nice, keep listening well,

00:04:10.367 --> 00:04:13.607
and keep being the boss
ladies that you are.

00:04:13.607 --> 00:04:15.207
Goodbye, this has been very fun.

00:04:15.207 --> 00:04:19.175
This has been a great
first vlogging experience.

00:04:19.175 --> 00:04:20.046
So, cut.

00:04:20.046 --> 00:04:23.213
(upbeat, happy music)

00:04:24.072 --> 00:04:25.497
(sign creaking)

